      "message": "test(kernel): add step_agreement verdict rows for bad_entity_mid_data and lathe_holder_offset\n\nBoth fixtures were added since v0.18.0 without a row in the expected\ntable. Measured verdicts (release, step_agreement):\n- bad_entity_mid_data.step: import both refuse by name (solidcore\n  read_step STEP syntax error), mesh no exact solid to judge against\n- lathe_holder_offset.step: import agree, mesh watertight within tolerance\nBoth are millimetre files (SI_UNIT MILLI METRE), so mm_per_unit 1.0,\nthe default the test already used for them. No fixture, golden or\nproduct code changed.\n\nFixes #1400\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
